# Native Face Pipeline

## Bundle layout

- `src/bin/face_pipeline.app/Contents/MacOS/face_pipeline` — macOS executable
- `src/bin/face_pipeline.app/Contents/Frameworks/*.dylib` — macOS runtime libs (`@executable_path/../Frameworks`)
- `src/bin/face_pipeline.app/Contents/Resources/models/` — macOS ONNX models (SCRFD, RF-DETR, optional OSNet)
- `src/bin/models/` — shared/Windows model root used in packaging

## Build flow (macOS)

1. `yarn build:native` — CMake + compile (`-DFACE_PIPELINE_ENABLE_GMC=OFF` by default)
2. `yarn stage:native:mac` — install to `src/bin`, run `scripts/stage-native-macos.sh` (emit `.app`, write `Info.plist`/`PkgInfo`, collect dylibs into `Contents/Frameworks`, rewrite install names, ad-hoc sign internals)
3. `yarn build` — CEP-only build; precheck validates native bundle
4. `yarn zxp` — runs `verify:native` first, then packages

## Release flow (macOS, Gatekeeper compliant)

- `yarn native:mac:release` — runs build + stage + verify + Developer ID sign + notarize + staple + Gatekeeper verification.
- `yarn verify:mac:dist` — validates Developer ID authority, Team ID, hardened runtime, timestamp, `spctl` acceptance, and stapled ticket.

## Key scripts

- `scripts/stage-native-macos.sh <exe> <out_dir>` — emits app bundle structure, relinks dylibs for `Contents/Frameworks`, and signs internals after install-name changes
- `scripts/verify-native-bundle.mjs` — checks `src/bin` structure
- `scripts/verify-macos-distribution.mjs` — checks Gatekeeper/notarization readiness
- `scripts/setup_onnx_models.sh` — fetches/copies ONNX models into `src/bin/models`

## GMC

- Default: translation-only fallback (no OpenCV)
- OpenCV GMC: `-DFACE_PIPELINE_ENABLE_GMC=ON` in CMake, `brew install opencv` — adds many dylibs

## Runtime

- CEP/Node spawns `face_pipeline.app/Contents/MacOS/face_pipeline`, passes frame paths via stdin
- No mac `DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH` requirement in app-bundle runtime path
